Here's what I did:

**`ReportGenerator.cs`** — Replaced `DateTime.UtcNow` with the built-in `TimeProvider` abstraction via primary constructor injection. Both call sites now use `timeProvider.GetUtcNow()`.

**`Program.cs`** — Registered `TimeProvider.System` (the real clock) as a singleton in DI.

**To test deterministically**, install `Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing` in your test project:

```csharp
var fakeTime = new FakeTimeProvider(
    new DateTimeOffset(2026, 1, 15, 10, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero));
var generator = new ReportGenerator(fakeTime);

var path = generator.GenerateReport("Sales");
Assert.Contains("20260115_100000", path);

fakeTime.Advance(TimeSpan.FromHours(1)); // control time in tests
```
